From 0a158ac483b8a8513fd05a566619cfed3f9f77ab Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tobias Fischer <info@tobiasfischer.info>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 20:55:44 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] Make TagLab usable from another working directory /
 embeddable

TagLab only worked when started from its own folder, and only through
`python TagLab.py`. Resources were opened with paths relative to the
current directory (icons, models, dictionaries; several icons even used
Windows backslashes, so they were missing on Linux and macOS), and
everything the program needs besides the TagLab widget itself lived under
`if __name__ == '__main__'`. Started from elsewhere the window had no
icons and a modal "dictionary not found" box blocked start-up; used from
another application, TagLab() raised NameError (slider_style2).

- genutils.TAGLAB_DIR / taglabPath() give the TagLab folder; icons,
  model weights, the default dictionary, the version file, the log and the
  classifier's temp folder are joined onto it
- slider_style1/2 are module level
- the application icon, style sheet and font are set by setupApplication(),
  which __main__ calls; an application that embeds TagLab does not have
  to adopt them
- TagLab(screen_size, check_updates=False) skips the online version
  check, which quits the process when a newer version exists on main
- a relative default dictionary stored in the settings is resolved
  against the TagLab folder

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
